{"at":"2026-10-18T02:14:55Z","digest":"sha256:026536394973151b3e35a94186d7106d5eaf4e72639ae302ccf778145cf9b3de","kind":"rejection","marker":"none","payload":{"answers":["sha256:ac103c6bdd13ec6558d7a44a3624a95f2ead2e12cd93357db5125cd96022787d"],"by":"owner-answer","job":"judge-1bdd9844da49e49e","reason":"capture-error","records":[{"hash":"sha256:8e10cf8c33d784957c62dab953b727b9d7e409e6d13d616625faf626efbeed4c","hypotheses":["The merge check into main refuses a landing whose result has a validate error not present at the merge base, or a link stale in the result but not at the base, and names each to the agent with the step that clears it (repin after tests, relink, or a card when the meaning changed). Links and errors already present at the base never hold the merge. The owner is asked nothing.","given a branch whose landing would add one validate error, when it merges into main, then the merge is refused naming the error, and the owner is asked nothing","given a branch that leaves SR-200's link to a file it changed stale, when it merges into main, then the merge is refused naming the link and saying repin after its tests pass","given a link already stale at the merge base, when a branch that does not touch it merges, then the merge is not held for it","given a branch adding no error and no stale link, when it merges, then the merge goes through"],"id":"SR-297","kind":"example-restatement","premise":""}],"session":"b766e5d7-5b6d-405d-bd71-03afe2c7dd47"},"prev":"sha256:b14ea6a0a4f100fbba38b931e76d39eb34d6fcabba752071f0ca65f16a082299","v":1}
